## Who needs what {#access-who}

This part explains how to reach the system from your own computer, step by step. It is written for {{ oses_shown | join(", ") | replace("windows", "Windows") | replace("macos", "macOS") | replace("linux", "Linux") }}.{% if win %} On Windows you type the commands in **PowerShell** (Start menu, type "PowerShell").{% endif %}{% if unix_os %} On {{ unix_label }} you type the commands in the **Terminal** app.{% endif %} Each step says what you want to do, what to type, what you should see, and what to do if it fails.

Commands marked *(not tested)* have not been tried on a real laptop yet. If one of them fails, tell the vendor.

Not everyone needs every part. Find your role in this table:

|                          | Viewer (web pages only)       | Operator (also servers)         | Successor (runs the installer)   |
|:-------------------------|:------------------------------|:--------------------------------|:---------------------------------|
| Tools                    | A browser, KeePassXC{{ ", an authenticator app" if f.admin_sso }} | The same, plus the SSH program{{ ", kubectl" if f.orchestrator == "k3s" }}; optional database tools | The same, plus git, Python 3.12 or newer, age; macOS or Linux only |
| Web pages                | Yes                           | Yes                             | Yes                              |
| SSH and tunnels          | No                            | Yes                             | Yes                              |
| Runs the installer       | No                            | No                              | Yes                              |

{% if people %}
The people named for this handover:

| Name                      | Role          | Laptop       | Internet address                  |
|:--------------------------|:--------------|:-------------|:----------------------------------|
{% for p in people %}
| {{ p.name | md if p.name else NP }} | {{ p.persona | capitalize if p.persona else NP }} | {{ osname.get(p.os, NP) if p.os else NP }} | {{ (p.allow_from | join(", ") | md) if p.allow_from else NP }} |
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
Before your first visit, the vendor does two things for you:

1. Adds your internet address to the allow-lists, if the lists are in use (see [Your internet address](#access-ip)).
2. Adds your SSH key to every server, if you are an operator (see [SSH](#access-ssh)).

