### Kubernetes (k3s) {#access-cluster-k3s}

Goal: use kubectl, the Kubernetes command, from your laptop. The cluster's API (port 6443) is closed to laptops, so kubectl goes through the SSH tunnel.

1. Install kubectl, within one minor version of k3s ({{ f.versions.k3s or NP }}).

{{ per_os("winget install -e --id Kubernetes.kubectl", "brew install kubectl", None) }}
{% if win %}
The winget package name is *(not tested)*.
{% endif %}
{% if "linux" in oses_shown %}
On Linux, install it with snap or the official binary from kubernetes.io.
{% endif %}

2. Copy the cluster's access file (kubeconfig). It is a secret: it gives full control of the cluster, so it stays on your laptop.

{{ cmds("mkdir -p ~/.kube\nssh " ~ mgr ~ " \"sudo cat /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml\" > ~/.kube/" ~ slug ~ ".yaml", "mkdir -Force $HOME\\.kube\nssh " ~ mgr ~ " \"sudo cat /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml\" |\n  Set-Content -Encoding ascii $HOME\\.kube\\" ~ slug ~ ".yaml") }}
{% if win %}
On Windows PowerShell 5.1, `>` writes a format kubectl cannot read, hence `Set-Content` *(not tested)*.
{% endif %}

3. Point it at the tunnel (port {{ tunnel_port("k3s") }} on your laptop):

{{ cmds("kubectl config set-cluster default --server=https://127.0.0.1:" ~ tunnel_port("k3s") ~ " \\\n  --kubeconfig ~/.kube/" ~ slug ~ ".yaml", "kubectl config set-cluster default --server=https://127.0.0.1:" ~ tunnel_port("k3s") ~ " `\n  --kubeconfig $HOME\\.kube\\" ~ slug ~ ".yaml") }}
4. Start the tunnel (`ssh -N {{ slug }}-tunnel`, see [the tunnel](#access-tunnel)) in its own window, then:

{{ cmds("kubectl --kubeconfig ~/.kube/" ~ slug ~ ".yaml get nodes", "kubectl --kubeconfig $HOME\\.kube\\" ~ slug ~ ".yaml get nodes") }}
**What you should see:** the servers, each with the status Ready.

**If it fails:** "connection refused" means the tunnel is not running. A certificate error means step 3 was skipped.
{% if f.database and f.database.ha %}

To reach the database through the cluster's database-proxy, which always points at the primary (use another laptop port while the tunnel runs, because {{ tunnel_port(f.database.app) }} is taken):

{{ cmds("kubectl --kubeconfig ~/.kube/" ~ slug ~ ".yaml -n ansibro \\\n  port-forward svc/database-proxy 25432:" ~ f.database.port, "kubectl --kubeconfig $HOME\\.kube\\" ~ slug ~ ".yaml -n ansibro `\n  port-forward svc/database-proxy 25432:" ~ f.database.port) }}
{% endif %}
