### Your own images {#access-cluster-images}

Goal: run your own app images. The image registry ({{ f.registry_addr }}) is reachable only from the servers, so you send the image over SSH and push it on the first server:

{{ cmds("docker save app:1 | ssh " ~ mgr ~ " \"sudo docker load\"\nssh " ~ mgr ~ " \"sudo docker tag app:1 " ~ f.registry_addr ~ "/app:1 && \\\n  sudo docker push " ~ f.registry_addr ~ "/app:1\"", "docker save app:1 | ssh " ~ mgr ~ " \"sudo docker load\"\nssh " ~ mgr ~ " (\"sudo docker tag app:1 " ~ f.registry_addr ~ "/app:1 && \" +\n  \"sudo docker push " ~ f.registry_addr ~ "/app:1\")") }}
`app:1` is your image name and version.{% if "macos" in oses_shown %} On a Mac with Apple Silicon, build the image with `--platform linux/amd64`: the servers use Intel or AMD processors.{% endif %} The registry is not in the backup: after a restore, push your images again.

